hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"201","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that when the delegation of ‘Abd al-Qays came, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Every person is accountable for his own self, and every nation may drink from those (vessels) which they find suitable.”"
"202","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I obtained this sermon by hearing it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and in it was also: ""Everything that is coming is near."
"203","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every eye is an adulterer."
"204","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything is by decree, even incapacity and intelligence (are by decree)."
"205","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said in a hadith: ""And every possessor of knowledge is hungry for knowledge."
"206","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “No act of worship to Allah has been performed that is superior to understanding (fiqh) in religion, and indeed, one jurist (faqih) is heavier against Satan than a thousand worshippers. And everything has a pillar, and the pillar of this religion is fiqh.” Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: “If I sit for an hour to acquire fiqh, it is more beloved to me than spending the night in worship from night until morning.”"
"207","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Everything has a pillar, and the pillar of this religion is jurisprudence (fiqh)."
"208","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything that causes confusion is forbidden, and there is nothing confusing in the religion."
"209","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you is a guardian, and each of you is responsible for those under his care."
"210","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, for every betrayer there will be a flag according to his betrayal."
"211","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, every betrayer will have a banner by which he will be recognized."" And Muslim has also narrated it with his chain: ""On the Day of Resurrection, every betrayer will have a banner according to his betrayal, by which he will be recognized."
"212","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the first matters to be decided among the people will be those of blood (i.e., murder)."
"213","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The first thing to be accounted for will be the prayer, and among the people, the first matter to be decided will be regarding bloodshed."
"214","It is narrated from Maymun bin Mehran that Sayyida Umm Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked, ""Have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" She said: ""Yes, I heard him say: '(On the Day of Judgment) the first thing to be placed in the scale will be good character.'"
"215","Dawud bin Abu Hind says that I passed by a warrior at the place of Jadilah, and he said: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first things to be taken away from this Ummah will be modesty and trustworthiness."
"216","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing you will lose from your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose is prayer."
"217","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing you will lose from your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose is prayer."
"218","Muhammad bin Talhah narrates from his father that indeed Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to a man who was called ‘Ufair: “What did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say?” He said: “I heard him, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ‘Love is also inherited and hatred is also inherited.’”"
"219","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “(Excessive) love for anything will make you blind and deaf.”"
"220","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A gift takes away hearing and sight."
"221","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness has been tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"222","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is in the foreheads of horses."
"223","Sayyiduna ‘Urwah al-Bariqi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Goodness has been tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"
"224","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blessing of horses is in their red color."
"225","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Travel is a portion of torment."
"226","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obeying women leads to regret."
"227","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Calamity is attached to speech."
"228","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Calamity is attached to speech."
"229","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is half of patience, and there is zakat on everything, and the zakat of the body is fasting."
"230","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of the fasting person is not rejected."
"231","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting in the winter is a cool booty."
"232","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Using the miswak increases a person's eloquence."
"233","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's beauty is in the eloquence of his tongue."
"234","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam is responsible (for the prayer), and the muezzin is entrusted (with the prayer time). O Allah! Guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."
"235","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the necks of the mu’adhdhins will be the longest of all."
"236","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My intercession is for those among my Ummah who commit major sins."
"237","I heard Qazi Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Salamah, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Abu al-Abbas Ahmad bin Husayn, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Abu al-Hasan Ahmad bin Abdur Rahman bin Bard, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Ibn Nafis, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Ali bin Muhammad bin Ismail, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Hudbah bin Khalid, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Abu Janab Qassab, swearing by Allah, say that he heard Ziyad al-Namiri, swearing by Allah, say that he heard our master Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), swearing by Allah, say that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""My intercession is for those among my Ummah who commit major sins."
"238","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ansar are my sincere companions and confidants."
"239","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah's hand is over the group (jama‘ah)."
"240","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Silence is wisdom, and those who practice it are very few."
"241","Sayyida Umm Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sustenance seeks a servant with even more intensity than death seeks him."
"242","Hajjaj bin Sulaiman Ru‘eeni says: I said to Ibn Lahi‘ah: Gentleness in livelihood is better than some kinds of trade. This is something I have heard my elderly women say. So he said: Muhammad bin Munkadir narrated to me from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Gentleness in livelihood is better than some kinds of trade.”"
"243","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The cowardly trader remains deprived, and the courageous trader attains (success)."
"244","Sayyiduna Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Good character is a means of progress and bad character is misfortune.”"
"245","Sayyiduna Rafi’ bin Makith, who was among the Companions present at Hudaybiyyah, narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: “Good character is a means of progress and bad character is misfortune. Righteousness is a cause of increase in age and charity prevents an evil death.”"
"246","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from his brother Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The disgrace of this world is lighter than the disgrace of the Hereafter."
"247","Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The grave is the first stage among the stages of the Hereafter."
"248","Sayyiduna ‘Uthman’s freed slave Hani’ reports that when Sayyiduna ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) would stand by a grave, he would weep so much that his beard would become wet. Hani’ says that it was said to him: “Paradise and Hell are mentioned before you, yet you do not weep (so much), but you weep (so much) at this (grave)?” So he said: “Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Indeed, the grave is the first stage among the stages of the Hereafter.’” And he narrated this hadith... And he narrated this hadith."
"249","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Patience is at the first stroke of calamity."
"250","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that when condolences were offered to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the death of his daughter, Sayyidah Ruqayyah (may Allah be pleased with her), who was the wife of Sayyiduna Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All praise is due to Allah; burying daughters (after death) is a cause of honor and dignity."
"251","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The battlefield of death is between sixty and seventy years (of age)."
"252","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The ages of my Ummah (people) will be between sixty and seventy years, and very few will exceed this."
"253","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deceives us is not from among us, and the one who practices deceit, trickery, and cheating will be in the Fire."
"254","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deceives us is not from among us, and the one who practices deceit, trickery, and cheating will be in the Fire."
"255","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A false oath lays houses to ruin."
"256","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A false oath may sell the goods, but it destroys the blessing of the earnings."
"257","This narration is also reported from Abdur Rahman bin Ya'qub Jahni through another chain in the same manner... and he narrated this hadith."
"258","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “A (false) oath may sell the goods, but it destroys the blessing.”"
"259","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The oath is according to the intention of the one who makes the other swear."
"260","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath is either broken or one has to feel ashamed of it."
"261","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath has to be broken or one becomes ashamed of it."
"262","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Salam is a gift for our community and a security for our dhimmis.”"
"263","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Knowledge from which no benefit is taken is like a treasure from which nothing is spent."
"264","The companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Sinan bin Sanah Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The one who eats food and gives thanks has a reward equal to that of the fasting person who is patient."
"265","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... And he mentioned it briefly... And he narrated this hadith."
"266","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between a servant and disbelief is (the act of) abandoning prayer."
"267","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between a servant and disbelief is (the act of) abandoning prayer."
"268","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The position of prayer in religion is like the position of the head in the body."
"269","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The reward for praying while sitting is half of the reward for praying while standing."
"270","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakat is the treasure of Islam."
"271","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The perfume for men is that whose color is hidden and whose fragrance spreads, and the perfume for women is that whose color is apparent and whose fragrance is hidden."
"272","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The fragrance for men is that whose color is hidden and whose scent spreads, and the fragrance for women is that whose color is apparent and whose scent is hidden."
"273","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soil is the delight of children."
"274","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Souls are like gathered armies; those who became acquainted with one another (in the realm of souls) feel affection for each other here (in the world), and those who remained unfamiliar with one another there are opposed to each other here."
"275","Abu Hurairah says that I asked Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both): What have you memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He said: I have memorized this (hadith) from him: ""Truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt."
"276","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an is wealth; after it there is no poverty, and without it there is no richness."" Darqutni says: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it as mursal from Al-A'mash, from Yazid Al-Raqashi, from Al-Hasan, and this is more correct."
"277","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Faith in destiny removes sorrow and grief.”"
"278","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Renunciation of the world brings comfort to the heart and body, and desire for the world increases sorrow and grief, and idleness hardens the heart."
"279","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The scholar and the learner are both partners in goodness, and the rest of the people are evil; there is no goodness in them."
"280","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand is responsible for what it has (borrowed) until it returns it."
"281","Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand is responsible for what it has (borrowed) until it returns it."
"282","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The child belongs to the one on whose bed he is born, and for the adulterer there is the stone."
"283","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The child belongs to the one on whose bed it is born, and for the adulterer there are stones."
"284","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hospitality is (obligatory) upon the villagers and not (obligatory) upon the townspeople."
"285","Sayyiduna Husayn ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The beggar has a right, even if he comes riding on a horse."
"286","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""What disease can be worse than miserliness?"
"287","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""What disease can be worse than miserliness?"
"288","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back what he has given as a gift is like a dog that licks up its own vomit. A bad example is not for us."
"289","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Looking at greenery increases eyesight, and looking at a beautiful woman also increases eyesight."
"290","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, my Ummah will come with their faces, hands, and feet shining from the marks of ablution."
"291","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Clapping is for women and saying Subhan Allah is for men.”"
"292","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gaze is one of the arrows from the arrows of Iblis. Whoever abandons it out of fear of Allah, Allah will grant him such faith, the sweetness of which he will feel in his heart."
"293","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (lustful) gaze is one of the poisonous arrows of Satan. Whoever abandons it out of fear of Me, I will grant him such faith whose sweetness he will feel in his heart."
"294","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is misfortune in a house, a horse, and a woman."
"295","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two blessings regarding which many people are in loss: (one is) health and (the other is) free time."
"296","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Destruction is for the Arabs because of an evil that has drawn near.”"
"297","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The honor of a believer is in his piety, his dignity is in his character, his lineage is in his religion, and cowardice and bravery are natural traits; Allah places them in whomever He wills.”"
"298","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity, concealing illnesses, and concealing misfortunes are among the treasures of goodness."
"299","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was once sitting in a tent when Sa’ib bin ‘Abd Yazid came to him, and with him was his son. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at both of them and said: “It is among a person’s good fortune that he resembles his father.”"
"300","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Good character is part of a person’s good fortune.”"
"301","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Those who are good in this world will be good in the Hereafter, and those who are evil in this world will be evil in the Hereafter.”"
"302","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The trustworthy treasurer who gives that which he has been commanded to give (in the way of Allah) with a cheerful heart, he too is counted among those who give charity."
"303","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The trustworthy treasurer who gives that which he has been commanded to give (in the way of Allah) with a cheerful heart, he too is counted among those who give charity."
"304","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The king is Allah's shade on the earth; every oppressed person seeks refuge with him."
"305","Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunais Makki says that we went to visit Sufyan Thawri during his illness, and Sa'id bin Hassan also came to visit him. Sufyan said to him: ""Tell me again the hadith that you narrated to me."" He said: Umm Salih narrated to me from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, who narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every word of the son of Adam is counted against him, not in his favor, except for enjoining good, forbidding evil, and the remembrance of Allah."
"306","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Deliberation in work, steadfastness, moderation, and silence are one twenty-sixth part of Prophethood.”"
"307","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The Prophets (peace be upon them) are leaders, the jurists are chiefs, and sitting in their gatherings is a cause of increase (in knowledge)."
"308","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""One who displays something which he does not own is like one who wears two garments of falsehood (a deceiver)."
"309","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who pretends to have what he has not been given is like one who wears a garment of falsehood."
"310","Musa bin Ja'far narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather with a connected chain of transmission, he said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Performing ablution before eating removes poverty, and performing ablution after eating erases minor sins and corrects the eyesight."
"311","Abadullah (Abdullah bin Umar, Abdullah bin Mas’ud, Abdullah bin Zubair, and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them) narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “The storyteller awaits the wrath (of Allah), and the one who listens to him awaits mercy. The trader awaits sustenance, and the hoarder awaits a curse. Upon the wailing woman and those women who gather around her to listen, is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"
"312","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “To live a long life in obedience to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is nothing but happiness.”"
"313","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jarad (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is overtaken by the Day of Resurrection (i.e., he had not died), his wretchedness is true wretchedness."
"314","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves his family and dependents with (unlawful) wealth and himself meets his Lord bearing sin, for him there is nothing but destruction upon destruction."
"315","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of the oppressed is accepted even if he is a sinner, because his sinfulness (the consequence of it) is upon himself."
"316","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Three (persons') supplications are (surely) accepted, there is no doubt in their acceptance: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a parent against his child."
"317","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are three types of judges: two are in Hell and one is in Paradise. The judge who gives a verdict contrary to what Allah has revealed is in Hell, and the judge who gives a verdict according to his desires is also in Hell, and the judge who gives a verdict according to what Allah has revealed is in Paradise.”"
"318","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two good qualities cannot be found in a hypocrite: good character and understanding in religion."
"319","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Two bad traits cannot be combined in a believer: miserliness and bad character."
"320","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from his father, Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Two kinds of eyes will not be touched by the (Hell) Fire: one eye that wept out of fear of Allah in the middle of the night, and the other eye that kept watch in the way of Allah during the night."
"321","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two kinds of eyes will not be touched by the Fire: one eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and the other eye that kept watch in the way of Allah."
"322","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two types of hungry, greedy people are never satisfied: one who seeks knowledge and the other who seeks the world."
"323","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An old man remains young in two things: in the love of a long life and in the love of abundance of wealth."
"324","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There are four types of people whom Allah dislikes: the one who sells goods by swearing oaths, the arrogant poor person, the old adulterer, and the unjust ruler."
"325","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Three things are destructive and three things are salvatory. The three destructive things are: miserliness which is obeyed, desires of the self which are followed, and a person being pleased with his own praise. And the three salvatory things are: fearing Allah in secret and in public, moderation in wealth and poverty, and acting justly in a state of happiness and anger."
"326","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Three things are destructive and three things are saving. So the three destructive things are: miserliness which is obeyed, desires of the self which are followed, and a person being pleased with his own praise. And the three saving things are: fearing Allah in secret and in public in every situation, adopting moderation in wealth and poverty (both conditions), and acting with justice and fairness in happiness and anger."
"327","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Three things are destructive and three things are saving. The three destructive things are: miserliness which is obeyed, desires of the soul which are followed, and a person being pleased with his own praise. And the three saving things are: fearing Allah in secret and in public, moderation in wealth and poverty, and acting justly in pleasure and in anger.”"
"328","Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whatever two people who abuse each other say, (its burden) will be upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed does not exceed the limits.”"
"329","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever two people who abuse each other say, (the burden of it) will be upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed does not exceed the limits."" And Muslim bin Hajjaj has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever two people who abuse each other say, (the burden of it) will be upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed does not exceed the limits."
"330","Ubaid bin Umair (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be ahead of you at the Hawd (Pond) on the Day of Resurrection."
"331","Sayyiduna Jundub bin Sufyan Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""I will be ahead of you at the Pond (Hawd) on the Day of Resurrection."
"332","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I and the one who takes care of an orphan will be in Paradise like this (close to each other).”"
"333","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""O Banu Hashim! O Banu Qusayy! I am a warner, death is a destroyer, and the Day of Resurrection is the appointed time."
"334","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever remained silent has attained salvation."
"335","Abis bin Rabi’ah reports that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said from the pulpit: “O people! Adopt humility, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Whoever adopts humility for the sake of Allah, Allah grants him elevation, so that he considers himself small in his own eyes while he is great in the eyes of the people. And whoever adopts arrogance, Allah the Mighty and Majestic makes him low, so that he considers himself great while he is small in the eyes of the people, until he becomes more despicable than a dog or a pig.’”"
"336","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I received this sermon from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at Tabuk, so I heard him say... And in a lengthy sermon, he also mentioned this matter... And he narrated this hadith."
"337","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say this, and he mentioned this also in a long hadith... And he narrated this hadith."
"338","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is thoroughly questioned in the reckoning will be punished."
"339","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to live in the wilderness becomes hard-hearted, whoever pursues hunting becomes heedless, and whoever goes to the doors of rulers falls into tribulation."
"340","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr."
"341","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his family is a martyr."
"342","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed while saving his life is also a martyr."
"343","Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr, and whoever is killed while protecting his family is also a martyr, and whoever is killed while protecting his religion is also a martyr."
"344","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for someone, He afflicts him with a hardship from Himself."
"345","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"346","Muhammad bin Ka'b says that Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said from the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Allah Almighty grants understanding of the religion to whomever He intends good for."" Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"347","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Qabeesah bin Dhu’ayb (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah Almighty, when He intends good for someone, makes his character good.”"
"348","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever longs for Paradise hastens towards good deeds, and whoever fears Hell becomes indifferent to desires, and whoever keeps death in mind becomes unconcerned with pleasures, and whoever is disinterested in the world finds calamities easy to bear."
"349","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies in a foreign land has died the death of a martyr."
"350","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever boasts over slaves, Allah Almighty will disgrace him."
"351","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! There should be no deception among Muslims. Whoever deceives us is not from us."" And Muslim bin Hajjaj has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever raises a weapon against us is not from us, and whoever deceives us is also not from us."
"352","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever deceives us is not from among us, and whoever raises a weapon against us is also not from among us."
"353","Sayyiduna Abu Hamra (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he passed by a man who had grain in a container. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards it and said: ""You have deceived. Whoever deceives us is not from among us."
"354","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deceives us is not from among us, and the one who practices trickery, fraud, and deceit is in the Fire."
"355","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow at us during the night is not one of us."
"356","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not trim his mustache is not one of us."
"357","Mu'tamir says that I heard Yusuf bin Suhaib narrate from Habib bin Yasar with his chain a hadith similar to this, and in its wording he said: ""Whoever does not trim his mustache."
"358","This hadith is also narrated from Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission... and he narrated this hadith."
"359","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever introduces into our matter (religion) something which does not belong to it, it is rejected."
"360","Ibrahim bin Sa’d narrated from his father with his chain of transmission a hadith similar to this one.......... and he narrated this hadith."
"361","Ibrahim bin Sa’d narrated a hadith similar to this with his chain of transmission........ And he narrated this hadith."
"362","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever acts with deliberation reaches (the truth) or comes close to it, and whoever acts with haste errs or comes close to erring.”"
"363","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever acts with deliberation reaches (the truth), or comes close to (the truth), and whoever acts with haste errs, or comes close to (error)."
"364","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sows goodness will reap the harvest of desire, and whoever sows evil will reap the harvest of regret."
"365","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sows goodness will reap the harvest of desire, and whoever sows evil will reap the harvest of regret."
"366","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... and in a long hadith he also mentioned this matter... and he narrated this hadith."
"367","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b that he said to Umar bin Abdul Aziz that our master Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated a hadith to us, saying that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said in a long hadith: ""And whoever wishes to be the most honorable among the people, let him fear Allah; and whoever wishes to be the strongest among the people, let him put his trust in Allah; and whoever wishes to be the richest and most affluent among the people, let him have more trust and certainty in what is with Allah than in what is in his own hand."
"368","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever wishes to be the most honorable among the people should fear Allah, and whoever wishes to be the richest among the people should place more trust and certainty in what is with Allah than in what is in his own hand."
"369","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends to commit a sin but then abandons it, for him there is one good deed. And whoever intends to commit a sin and then acts upon it, then seeks forgiveness from Allah, he will be forgiven."
"370","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever Allah grants wealth, it should certainly be apparent on him, and it is obligatory for him to begin with his dependents, and whatever remains should be returned towards (other) needy people. Do not blame the one who is content, and do not consider yourself incapable."
"371","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever likes to remain safe should adhere to silence.”"
"372","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever speaks much will make many mistakes, and whoever makes many mistakes will have many sins, and whoever has many sins is more deserving of the Hellfire. Listen! Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”"
"373","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever speaks much will make many mistakes, and whoever makes many mistakes will have many sins, and whoever has many sins is more deserving of the Hellfire. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."
"374","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever speaks much will make many mistakes, and whoever speaks much will lie much, and whoever lies much will have many sins, and whoever has many sins is most deserving of Hell.” Abu Ahmad said: I think this hadith is a mistake, because this statement is only narrated from Sayyiduna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). I have memorized it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) only with this chain. As for the narration of Umar, Ibn Durayd narrated it to us with his chain from Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said that Umar said to me: O Ahnaf! Whoever laughs much, his awe diminishes, and whoever jokes excessively is considered insignificant, and whoever is excessive in anything becomes known for it. And whoever speaks much, his mistakes are many, and whoever makes many mistakes, his modesty decreases, and whoever’s modesty decreases, his piety decreases, and whoever’s piety decreases, his heart dies and his death comes suddenly."
"375","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever receives sustenance through any means should adhere to it.”"
"376","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever a blessing is bestowed upon, he should give thanks for it."
"377","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: “Whoever does not give thanks for a little, will not give thanks for much, and whoever does not thank people, does not thank Allah.”"
"378","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever consoles a person afflicted by a calamity will have a reward equal to that of the afflicted one.”"
"379","This hadith is also narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission in the same manner... and the hadith was narrated in the same way."
"380","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever consoles a person afflicted by a calamity, for him is a reward equal to that (afflicted) person."
"381","This hadith is also narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Muhammad bin Sawqah... and the hadith was narrated in the same way."
"382","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives iftar to a fasting person, he will have a reward equal to that (fasting person)."
"383","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever is gentle with my Ummah, Allah Almighty will be gentle with him, and whoever is harsh with my Ummah, Allah Almighty will be harsh with him.”"
"384","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever visits a sick person will always remain in the khurfa of Paradise.” It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the khurfa of Paradise? He replied: “Its fruits.”"
"385","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person remains in the harvest of Paradise until he returns."
"386","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever supplicates against his oppressor has indeed taken retribution for his oppression."
"387","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever supplicates against his oppressor has indeed taken retribution for the oppression done to him."
"388","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever supplicates against his oppressor has indeed taken retribution for (the oppression)."
"389","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever walks with an oppressor has indeed committed a crime."" Allah the Exalted says: «بے شک ہم مجرموں سے انتقام لینے والے ہیں۔»"
"390","Tawoos reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever imitates a people is one of them."
"391","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever acquires knowledge, Allah becomes responsible for his sustenance."
"392","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not benefit from his knowledge, his ignorance will harm him. Recite the Qur'an; it will restrain you. If it does not restrain you, then (it is as if) you have not recited it at all."
"393","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He whom his deeds hold back, his lineage will not push him forward."" And in Ibn Jami’'s hadith, instead of «لم يسرع» , the words «لا يسرع» are used."
"394","Muhammad bin Ja'far, narrating with his chain of transmission, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever sets out on a path in search of knowledge, Allah will lead him on a path to Paradise. And whoever is left behind by his knowledge, his lineage will not bring him forward."
"395","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is appointed as a judge, indeed he has been slaughtered without a knife."" This hadith is also in Fawa'id Ibn al-A'rabi, and in it is: ""So indeed he has been slaughtered without a knife."" And in the hadith of Za'farani, the word ""faqad"" (indeed) is not present. And I have seen it in the Mu'jam of the shuyukh of Sufyan Thawri, with the chain of 'Ammarah bin Ghaziyyah from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurairah, and they have narrated it as marfu' and in it the word ""faqad"" (indeed) is present."
"396","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever is appointed to the position of judge has truly been slaughtered without a knife."
"397","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever carries his own load has indeed freed himself from arrogance."
"398","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever adopts a harsh way in this religion, then this (religion) will overpower him."
"399","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever denies intercession will not attain it on the Day of Resurrection."
"400","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed, then he is a believer."
